    "Input and display AST resolvers both use a shared formatter helper with selected-item decimal_type nullish fallback; no-option path uses default format",
    "Common digit helper instead looks at $exchange first with external emptiness fallback; this helper and subscriber do not establish one universal precedence",
    "Common render-item resolver distinguishes code zero from domestic by matching registered zero-code options, with last-vs-first lookup by foreign flag; do not map own KRW conventions mechanically",
